  "summary": "Updates `doc/i2p.md` to document the minimum compatible versions of Java I2P (≥ 2.10.0) and i2pd (≥ 2.58.0). It adjusts the Compatibility section, which previously claimed any SAM v3.1 router could be used.",
  "problem": "Documentation currently misinforms users that any SAM v3.1 router works with Bitcoin Core, even though PR #35696 introduced a dependency on leaseSet encryption types (`i2cp.leaseSetEncType=6,4`) that older routers do not support.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"In `doc/i2p.md`, the Compatibility section stated that any SAM v3.1 router can be used. Bitcoin Core now relies on a feature that requires recent routers: `i2cp.leaseSetEncType=6,4` (introduced in #35696). This is supported by Java I2P ≥ 2.10.0 and i2pd ≥ 2.58.0.\""
